                <pb facs="0403" n="391" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg391"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115 PW/8–245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-08T20:00:00-04:00">August 8, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2492. Inform Swiss that Department is seriously concerned by use of term hostage
                    in your 3777 August 2. Suggestion has been made by a reliable neutral long
                    resident in Tokyo that Japanese savagery might be vented upon POWs as war goes
                    against Japan. Department desires to receive any information Swiss may receive
                    in this regard.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
